# Keep shell scripts LF. core.autocrlf is true on this machine, so without this
# a fresh checkout hands Git Bash a CRLF build-corpus.sh and every line fails
# with "$'\r': command not found" -- in the tree where these scripts are
# actually RUN, not just stored. The public mirror pins the same rule.
*.sh text eol=lf
# Normalize everything else by default.
* text=auto

# Vendored upstream BaseX files — keep them BYTE-IDENTICAL to the distribution.
# LICENSE is the BSD-3-Clause notice we are required to reproduce in order to
# redistribute BaseX.jar at all, so it must not be line-ending-normalised on the
# way through a Windows checkout (autocrlf is on here). The jar is detected as
# binary anyway; saying so is cheaper than relying on the detection.
basex/LICENSE -text
basex/.basexhome -text
basex/BaseX.jar binary
